        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='7800' id='65' type-v2='text' w='95455' x='1364' y='24600'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontsize='11'>In the following table we will see the general improvement of the metrics for each experiment. You will see three different colors:</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontsize='11'>• green: there is a statistically significant improvement in the metric.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontsize='11'>• gray: there isn&apos;t any statistically significant change in the metric.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontsize='11'>• red: there is a statistically significant worsten in the metric.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontsize='11'>* This change was implemented on 2023-05-26, so all tests that were done before this date will have  either green color (significant change) or gray color (no significant change) for the metrics.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
